  body: |
    # Source-described delayed claims caused by specified overseas employment

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source gives a claim-timing provision for the named mariner, airman, continental shelf worker and forces categories, where overseas employment prevents a timely claim and the claim is made as soon as reasonably practicable.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 078100 is conditional on both the employment-related impediment and prompt subsequent action. It is not an unlimited overseas deadline extension or a rule for every claimant abroad.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 078100, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a7f779940f0b6230268fabd/dmgch0707.pdf#page=9)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is a model-assisted, unreviewed interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP source. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable rule. No specialist acceptance, current-law reconciliation or complete coverage of this chapter part is claimed. References to EU law, countries and benefits retain the scope and date context of the cited text; they do not establish applicability to a person or a later regime. Machine extraction may alter reading order and characters; no visual PDF review is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:20.233458Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication or legal commencement date. The attachment publication date is not established by the frozen metadata. Source-stated dates require their own role and precision.

