  - target: term/intl-mariner-other-benefits
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The conditional claim-timing paragraph explicitly names mariners among the special employment categories.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol2-ch7-part7/0009
      quote: "078100    A claim for benefit made by a mariner, airman, continental shelf worker or member\n                      1\n          of the forces is treated as made within the prescribed time if that person\n\n          1.    is outside the United Kingdom because of that employment and unable to\n                claim within the prescribed time and\n\n          2.    claims as soon as is reasonably practicable.\n                          1 SS (Mariners' Ben) Regs, reg 9; SS (Airmen's Ben) Regs, reg 3; SS (II) (Mariners' Ben) Regs,\n                                                 reg 8; SS (II) (Airmen's Ben) Regs, reg 5; SS Ben (PA) Regs, reg 11(4);\n                                                                           SS (Ben) (Members of the Forces) Regs, reg 5"
      locator: DMG 078100
